[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Expressive Launcher 4.1.2 (Build 61) — Expressive Core & Stable Drawer Sizing[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Official Release Announcement & Download Links[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

Two major milestones in this release: introducing [B]Expressive Core[/B] for frictionless browser installs on Android 15/16/17, and stabilizing app drawer icon sizing when exiting search. Thank you to our community contributors for reporting edge cases and testing!

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's New & Improved[/B][/SIZE]

1. [B]Expressive Core Edition[/B] (XDA-021):
[LIST]
[*]New lightweight build without Accessibility or Notification Listener services, specifically avoiding Google Play Protect's "Enhanced Fraud Protection" warning when sideloading from browsers.
[*]Built with the identical package name ([ICODE]dev.launcher.expressive.l3[/ICODE]) and signing certificate, ensuring seamless upgrades between Full and Core builds.
[*]Core provides standard home launcher features with device-admin or root screen lock fallbacks.

[/LIST]
2. [B]Stable Drawer Icon Sizing on Search Exit[/B] (TG-011):
[LIST]
[*]Fixed an issue where app drawer icons remained enlarged after backing out of drawer search and only reverted to proper proportions upon closing and reopening the drawer.
[*]In [ICODE]BubbleTextView[/ICODE], [ICODE]applyFromWorkspaceItem()[/ICODE] now synchronizes icon dimensions with the active [ICODE]AllAppsProfile[/ICODE] across drawer displays (prediction rows and search shortcuts).
[*]In [ICODE]ActivityAllAppsContainerView[/ICODE], completing search dismissal explicitly notifies active drawer adapters to refresh visible views against active device profile dimensions.

[/LIST]
3. [B]Dual-Variant QA Automation & CI Pipeline[/B] (XDA-021):
[LIST]
[*]Jenkins pipeline now automatically compiles, verifies, seals, and distributes Expressive Core ([ICODE]-PexpressiveCore=true[/ICODE]) alongside Full QA builds.
[*]Manifest scanner strictly validates that Core APKs contain no flagged permissions, and smoke tests verify upgrade compatibility between Full and Core releases.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Community Notes[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]App Drawer Search Sizing[/B]: Special thanks to Pratik for flagging the icon sizing discrepancy when navigating between search and the drawer!
[*][B]Play Protect Warnings[/B]: Thanks to our XDA community members for reporting sideload blocks under enhanced fraud protection rules!

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

I carry the heart of the launcher with pride, yet leave the heavy listeners outside. Play Protect smiles and lets me slide right in. What edition am I?
[SPOILER="Click to reveal the answer"]Expressive Core! 🛡️⚡[/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

